# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CODEOWNERS — who is requested to review changes by path.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The line below makes @humoge7502 the default owner for EVERY file in the
# repository: any PR touching a path without a more specific rule requests
# review from the owner. This is the correct setup for a single-maintainer
# project — nothing merges without maintainer review, and branch protection
# can enforce it (Settings → Branches → Protect `main` → require review
# from Code Owners).
#
# When the team grows, add more-specific rules BELOW the wildcard — later
# (more specific-path) entries take precedence, e.g.:
#   /contracts/            @humoge7502 @solidity-reviewer
#   /backend/              @humoge7502 @backend-reviewer
#   /frontend/             @humoge7502 @frontend-reviewer
#   /sdk/                  @humoge7502 @python-reviewer
#   /inspector/            @humoge7502 @python-reviewer
#   /planner/              @humoge7502 @ml-reviewer
#   /.github/workflows/    @humoge7502            # automation changes are sensitive
#   /docs/                 @humoge7502 @docs-reviewer
#
# SECURITY NOTE: CODEOWNERS files can live at repo root or in .github/ or
# docs/ — GitHub uses the first found. Keep exactly one to avoid ambiguity.
# A team name (@q-trust/core) can replace usernames once an org exists.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

* @humoge7502
